Z||000000||otis||02-09-2000||06:09 PM||||I have seen a blip on this  site on a<BR>previous message regarding  an annoying<BR>engine shudder at part throttle at<BR>speeds between 35  and 40 mph. The engine<BR>drops to 1500 rpm and the shudder starts.<BR>This is similar to  what happens when I<BR>lug my 4spd GT down by shifting into<BR>4th gear  with to low of engine rpm.<BR>I had this happen recently with my other<BR>86GT that  has an auto trans. I was in <BR>traffic and unable to speed up  to forty<BR>mph. I had  partial throttle and the engine<BR>rpm's dropped but speed ramined constant<BR>and the shudder  began. I think Ogre  may<BR>have mentioned this  in a reply he wrote<BR>regarding  another topic. Any ideas? Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||02-09-2000||06:33 PM||||lugging in high gear at low speed is farily common with manual transmisions. the exact speed it happens at depends on the motor, tranny and final gearing, and tires. It's the cars way of telling you to try downshifting a gear. Even automatic tranny will do it at times when you hover just above the shift point...||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||02-09-2000||06:54 PM||||I'm a bit confused... (nothing new  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>Is this problem with an Auto or Stick car???<P>On an Auto, couldn't this be caused by a faulty or misadjusted kickdown cable (or whatever you call the cable that runs from the throttle to the trans)??? Isn't this cable what "tells" the trans that you are lugging it?<P>||||reg||1
